LAN Notify project: Python + Tkinter local-network notification app with a TCP JSON server/client architecture. Server tracks connected users and usernames/IPs. Client has connection, username, and main GUI frames; saves host, port, and username to config.json; supports custom/empty notifications; received notifications trigger both native OS notification (Windows/Linux, optional dependencies) and Tkinter messagebox; window is brought to foreground. Project uses packages (client, server, shared) and is launched with python -m client.main and python -m server.main. Keep implementation simple and prioritize working code over premature complexity.
